Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Magandang hapon, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000242
00:32:44.600 --> 00:32:49.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Magandang hapon, Secretary Teodoro, sa lahat po ng ating kasama sa Armed Forces of the Philippines.

asr-000243
00:32:51.700 --> 00:32:53.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Talaga pong mabilis pong nagbabalik.

asr-000244
00:32:53.580 --> 00:32:58.820
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pabago ang geopolitical situation dito sa ating region at sa buong mundo na rin.

asr-000245
00:32:59.440 --> 00:33:05.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nakikita po natin yung iba't ibang mga conflict na nangyari sa Middle East,

asr-000246
00:33:05.700 --> 00:33:10.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: sa Eastern Europe, at sa iba pang parte ng buong mundo.

asr-000247
00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:15.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At sa ganitong punto, importante po na maging handa tayo

asr-000248
00:33:15.440 --> 00:33:20.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: at patuloy po natin minomodernize at pinapalakas po ang ating Armed Forces.

asr-000249
00:33:20.520 --> 00:33:23.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasama na rin po dito yung pagdating po sa cyber warfare.

asr-000250
00:33:23.580 --> 00:33:28.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Marami rin po akong pabalitaan at napapanood po sa balita

asr-000251
00:33:28.720 --> 00:33:39.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: na ang cyber warfare ay isa po sa mga bagay na nagiging realidad na sa mga ganito pong sitwasyon.

asr-000252
00:33:40.480 --> 00:33:44.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Alam ko, komplikado po itong cyberspace pero ganun pa man,

asr-000253
00:33:44.620 --> 00:33:53.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: importante na nakakabili [unclear] po tayo ng mga

asr-000254
00:33:53.580 --> 00:34:02.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kagamitan na makakatulong po tayo sa pagprepara sa mga ganitong conflicts at warfare.

asr-000255
00:34:03.740 --> 00:34:13.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At sa kabilang punto, ang Armed Forces of the Philippines ay hindi lang tag-defend ng ating bansa

asr-000256
00:34:13.300 --> 00:34:18.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kung hindi rin rin meresponder ito sa mga kalamidad na nangyayari po sa ating bansa.

asr-000257
00:34:18.940 --> 00:34:23.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At isa rin po sa mga bagay na dapat po natin tignan,

asr-000258
00:34:23.580 --> 00:34:31.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: multi-role capability ng ating armed forces, lalo na pag tumatama sa ating malaking bagyo

asr-000259
00:34:31.200 --> 00:34:35.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: o mayroong mga malalaking kalamidad na nararanasan natin.

asr-000260
00:34:36.220 --> 00:34:44.120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So kami po ay sumusuporta sa pagbibigay ng dagdag kapasidad ng ating armed forces

asr-000261
00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:49.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: at importante rin po na tuloy-tuloy yung supporta, sustainable yung pagsusuporta natin

asr-000262
00:34:49.540 --> 00:34:53.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: hanggat umabot tayo sa kakayahan na gusto natin makita.

asr-000263
00:34:53.580 --> 00:34:54.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So maraming salamat, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000264
00:34:55.820 --> 00:35:02.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, our Senate President. Maraming salamat din sa supporta mo nung isang taon sa ating armed forces.

asr-000265
00:35:02.820 --> 00:35:06.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The biggest ever, probably, budget for the AFP modernization.

asr-000266
00:35:06.860 --> 00:35:08.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our colleague, Senator Panfilo Lacson.

asr-000267
00:35:09.960 --> 00:35:16.420
Senator Panfilo "Ping" M. Lacson: None from this representation. I'll just listen to the presentation and seek clarification if I need to. Thank you.

asr-000268
00:35:16.780 --> 00:35:18.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Lacson, Senator Tulfo.

asr-000269
00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:22.340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Magandang araw po sa ating lahat.

asr-000270
00:35:22.340 --> 00:35:28.760
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Today, as we deliberate the proposed 2027 budget of the Department of National Defense,

asr-000271
00:35:29.180 --> 00:35:37.480
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: let us be guided by our commitment to protect our sovereignty, uphold our territorial integrity,

asr-000272
00:35:38.460 --> 00:35:41.220
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and ensure the safety and security of every Filipinos.

asr-000273
00:35:42.940 --> 00:35:48.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: But how can we do that if the budget of the National Defense is cut down,

asr-000274
00:35:48.300 --> 00:35:52.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: if I'm not mistaken, about 43.01%?

asr-000275
00:35:52.340 --> 00:35:57.620
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Bapano po natin mapoprotektahan ang ating soberenya,

asr-000276
00:35:58.780 --> 00:36:01.020
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: pagtatanggol po ang ating teritoryo,

asr-000277
00:36:01.740 --> 00:36:07.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: at masiguro ang siguridad at kapakanan ng bawat Pilipino kung binawasan po ng budget?

asr-000278
00:36:09.100 --> 00:36:11.340
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ang budget na ito ay hindi lamang tungkol sa numbers and allocations.

asr-000279
00:36:12.080 --> 00:36:18.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: It represents our investment in stronger, more capable, and more modern armed forces of the Philippines.

asr-000280
00:36:19.020 --> 00:36:22.280
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ang bawat pisong inilalaan sa pambansang depensa ay dapat,

asr-000281
00:36:22.340 --> 00:36:24.420
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: magsilbi sa kapakanan ng sambayan ng Pilipino.

asr-000282
00:36:25.260 --> 00:36:31.160
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Every allocation must translate into tangible improvements in our country's defense, posture,

asr-000283
00:36:31.780 --> 00:36:37.940
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: operational readiness, and ability to respond to both traditional emerging security challenges.

asr-000284
00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:41.120
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Nabawasan nga po ang external threat.

asr-000285
00:36:42.220 --> 00:36:49.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Ang ating internal threat, tumaas naman po ang external threat, meaning kalaban galing sa labas.

asr-000286
00:36:49.760 --> 00:36:52.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: How do we address that kung mas maliit po na budget?

asr-000287
00:36:53.060 --> 00:36:57.300
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We also recognize that national defense goes beyond preparedness.

asr-000288
00:36:58.240 --> 00:37:01.640
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: It encompasses our commitment to our soldiers and their families,

asr-000289
00:37:01.740 --> 00:37:05.140
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: our support for communities affected by conflict and disasters,

asr-000290
00:37:05.320 --> 00:37:08.800
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and our contribution to a peaceful, secure, and resilient Philippines.

asr-000291
00:37:09.500 --> 00:37:14.540
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: We look forward to a constructive discussion of DND's 2027 proposed budget

asr-000292
00:37:14.540 --> 00:37:19.700
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: to ensure that every peso strategically allocated, responsibly spent,

asr-000293
00:37:19.700 --> 00:37:22.200
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: and aligned with our national defense priorities.

asr-000294
00:37:22.340 --> 00:37:24.400
Senator Erwin T. Tulfo: Maraming salamat po, Gen. Chairman.

asr-000295
00:37:26.300 --> 00:37:27.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Tulfo.

asr-000296
00:37:29.600 --> 00:37:34.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Before we ask the Department of National Defense and the AFP for the presentation,

asr-000297
00:37:34.980 --> 00:37:38.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I seek the indulgence of our colleagues to allow the department and the touch agency

asr-000298
00:37:38.420 --> 00:37:41.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to conclude their presentation before asking questions.

asr-000299
00:37:42.040 --> 00:37:45.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Each center will be allowed later with about 10 minutes for questions.

asr-000300
00:37:46.420 --> 00:37:50.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In keeping tradition, of course, we will give priority to the officials of the Senate,

asr-000301
00:37:50.980 --> 00:37:51.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: followed by the centers.

asr-000302
00:37:52.340 --> 00:37:53.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In the order of the arrival.

asr-000303
00:37:54.140 --> 00:38:00.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So at this point, at this juncture, I would like now to call to our Secretary of National Defense,

asr-000304
00:38:00.100 --> 00:38:05.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Gilbert Teodoro, Jr., to deliver his opening statement and the presentation of the department

asr-000305
00:38:05.440 --> 00:38:06.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and its attached agencies thereafter.

asr-000306
00:38:07.240 --> 00:38:07.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-000307
00:38:08.100 --> 00:38:10.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Secretary Teodoro, you now have the floor.

asr-000308
00:38:10.880 --> 00:38:16.560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you very much, Mr. Chairperson, and to our Senate President and our sponsor last year,

asr-000309
00:38:16.980 --> 00:38:22.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to our Senator Lacson, Vice Chairman, and Senator Tulfo, Vice Chairman, likewise.

asr-000310
00:38:22.340 --> 00:38:30.540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is indeed an honor to present our budget request once again to this honorable chamber.

asr-000311
00:38:31.680 --> 00:38:41.860
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And might I just give a short preface and then if with the indulgence of the senators,

asr-000312
00:38:42.920 --> 00:38:52.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: go straight to page 15 of the presentation, which is the highlights of the proposed budget per NET.

asr-000313
00:38:52.340 --> 00:39:22.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Firstly, we, the Armed Forces of the Philippines, at the forefront together with the Department of National Defense in cooperation with other agencies, have been at the forefront of external defense operations in order to deter further aggression in the West Philippine Sea and other areas now not traditionally encompassed.

asr-000314
00:39:22.340 --> 00:39:32.360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, there still is robust presence to preserve the gains of internal security

asr-000315
00:39:32.360 --> 00:39:38.680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in areas which have been cleared of the CPP, NPA, and DF threat.

asr-000316
00:39:39.160 --> 00:39:47.420
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nonetheless, we estimate that robust presence of the Armed Forces of the Philippines,

asr-000317
00:39:47.420 --> 00:39:52.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: considering that the coverage of the Armed Forces of the Philippines,

asr-000318
00:39:52.340 --> 00:39:58.460
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: not only for operational purposes, but also for administrative and logistical purposes,

asr-000319
00:39:59.060 --> 00:40:04.840
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: is not as robust within the 7,600 islands as we want.

asr-000320
00:40:06.240 --> 00:40:14.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For this reason, the Philippine Army has been tasked to scope its areas of operations

asr-000321
00:40:14.120 --> 00:40:19.980
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and also to determine for logistical and staging purposes

asr-000322
00:40:19.980 --> 00:40:22.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and support purposes for our military.

asr-000323
00:40:22.160 --> 00:40:25.580
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For our strategic basing, which we have proposed,

asr-000324
00:40:26.540 --> 00:40:33.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: it is necessary to establish new presence, whether these be brigades or divisions.

asr-000325
00:40:33.960 --> 00:40:39.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, these areas will serve as nodes for our critical infrastructure,

asr-000326
00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:43.060
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which has to be, as we determined, stand-alone.

asr-000327
00:40:44.300 --> 00:40:49.440
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: You mentioned earlier our cyber systems.

asr-000328
00:40:50.140 --> 00:40:51.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We do have capabilities.

asr-000329
00:40:52.160 --> 00:41:02.300
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: However, these rely on the, shall we say,

asr-000330
00:41:02.460 --> 00:41:07.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sterile nature of critical basic infrastructure,

asr-000331
00:41:07.320 --> 00:41:12.280
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which we have had to remediate and deal with.

asr-000332
00:41:12.520 --> 00:41:19.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: As you know, in terms of IT, you start with IT and then you progress to cyber

asr-000333
00:41:19.760 --> 00:41:21.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: because your IT foundation is...

asr-000334
00:41:22.160 --> 00:41:26.540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the basis of your resilience and stability.

asr-000335
00:41:26.900 --> 00:41:32.380
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And one compromise in any area can lead to systemic compromises in others.

asr-000336
00:41:33.100 --> 00:41:36.340
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: This we had to continue to remediate.

asr-000337
00:41:36.960 --> 00:41:39.960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And as we construct our new infrastructure,

asr-000338
00:41:39.960 --> 00:41:47.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: we will incorporate the resilience necessary in these areas.

asr-000339
00:41:48.460 --> 00:41:50.700
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For our Navy,

asr-000340
00:41:52.160 --> 00:41:57.900
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the major thrust once again is not only for the new platforms

asr-000341
00:41:57.900 --> 00:42:04.100
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to complement with the Coast Guard our presence in the 360-degree area,

asr-000342
00:42:04.560 --> 00:42:13.220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: but we have a big gap which we are starting to fill hopefully by the end of this year

asr-000343
00:42:14.060 --> 00:42:18.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in our dockyards and our berthing facilities.

asr-000344
00:42:19.080 --> 00:42:21.960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Our naval bases,

asr-000345
00:42:22.160 --> 00:42:24.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: our design,

asr-000346
00:42:24.160 --> 00:42:28.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: except for a few,

asr-000347
00:42:28.160 --> 00:42:30.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: very few,

asr-000348
00:42:30.160 --> 00:42:32.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: are not deep nor big enough

asr-000349
00:42:32.160 --> 00:42:36.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to support the type of operations that we will need.

asr-000350
00:42:36.160 --> 00:42:40.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thirdly, our Philippine Air Force continues.

asr-000351
00:42:40.160 --> 00:42:49.060
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's the sustainment of the systems already ordered

asr-000352
00:42:49.060 --> 00:42:51.060
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and the upgrade of those systems.

asr-000358
00:42:52.920 --> 00:43:00.960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because we have to upgrade these systems while we try to segue,

asr-000359
00:43:02.040 --> 00:43:03.480
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: or to not segue,

asr-000360
00:43:03.480 --> 00:43:11.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to complement this with platforms that we can afford in the meantime,

asr-000361
00:43:12.500 --> 00:43:16.100
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which provide a sufficient deterrence for us.

asr-000362
00:43:19.100 --> 00:43:20.680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The Philippine Marine Corps,

asr-000363
00:43:20.680 --> 00:43:34.620
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We have a new commandant here, Brigadier General Apostol, who was tasked to scope the areas which need marine operations,

asr-000364
00:43:34.820 --> 00:43:40.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: knowing very well that the Philippine Marine Corps is a maneuver corps.

asr-000365
00:43:40.640 --> 00:43:42.600
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is not a territorial corps.

asr-000366
00:43:42.600 --> 00:43:57.340
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And with three marine brigades and one support brigade, no, four infantry brigades and one support brigade for 7,600 islands,

asr-000367
00:43:57.540 --> 00:44:02.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think just the math alone shows that it is too small.

asr-000368
00:44:02.880 --> 00:44:12.540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, the Air Force or the Navy or them must ensure their mobility and must ensure their firepower.

asr-000369
00:44:12.600 --> 00:44:17.800
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because a fixed marine unit is not a marine unit.

asr-000370
00:44:18.460 --> 00:44:24.800
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Its essence is its deployability and mobility.

asr-000371
00:44:24.800 --> 00:44:35.200
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, Brigadier General Apostol, once he is confirmed, Your Honors, hopefully soon,

asr-000372
00:44:36.280 --> 00:44:41.800
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: will devote his time to the...

asr-000373
00:44:42.600 --> 00:44:47.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ...growth plan of the Philippine Marine Corps that includes equipment.

asr-000374
00:44:49.080 --> 00:44:52.940
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We have talked about the internal security dimension,

asr-000375
00:44:53.940 --> 00:45:00.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: but a lot of operations right now have seen the connection between territorial...

asr-000376
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:24.780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: defense and internal security. That is in the front of illegal, FIMI and other illegal activities by undesirable state adversaries that have been proliferating, as the Senate President knows, in our space.

asr-000377
00:45:24.780 --> 00:45:54.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Which serve to weaken economic resilience, connectivity, and basic infrastructure, and perhaps other forms of malign activity, which we continued in coordination with other, with the law enforcement agencies to disrupt and to discuss.

asr-000378
00:45:54.780 --> 00:46:12.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think that is a major issue right now on internal security of which we devote a lot of cooperative time with the lead agencies, namely the PAO, the NBI.

asr-000379
00:46:15.720 --> 00:46:20.580
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: In HADR, of course, it is a constant threat.

asr-000380
00:46:20.580 --> 00:46:24.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: However, we have refined our deliverables now.

asr-000381
00:46:24.780 --> 00:46:29.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: To a coordinated response as quick as possible.

asr-000382
00:46:29.980 --> 00:46:40.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we concentrate on that in the OCD so that we do not lose focus on what people need immediately.

asr-000383
00:46:41.160 --> 00:46:50.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because feeling that need alone for those who may be displaced is already a very, very tall task.

asr-000384
00:46:50.160 --> 00:46:54.720
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And to exceed that will eat into the competence.

asr-000385
00:46:54.780 --> 00:47:06.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Of the other agencies, which should be doing resilience and other foundational efforts.

asr-000386
00:47:06.500 --> 00:47:23.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So we try to balance the need to focus, the need to coordinate with the ability also to coordinate international cooperation.

asr-000387
00:47:24.780 --> 00:47:30.140
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For collective resilience on the veteran side.

asr-000388
00:47:31.620 --> 00:47:34.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We continue to innovate.

asr-000389
00:47:35.740 --> 00:47:49.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Services to our veterans, which not only will be in terms of payment, but in terms of giving them.

asr-000390
00:47:49.240 --> 00:47:52.520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Wellness and dignity.

asr-000391
00:47:52.880 --> 00:47:54.700
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So that they can continue.

asr-000392
00:47:54.780 --> 00:48:01.780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: To continue their lives after they have served in a manner which fits their service.

asr-000393
00:48:01.780 --> 00:48:23.060
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The Veterans Memorial Medical Center, as we said, your honors, now has what we call the Valor Clinics to disaggregate basic medical services throughout the country.

asr-000394
00:48:23.060 --> 00:48:24.700
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So that the veterans.

asr-000395
00:48:24.780 --> 00:48:29.720
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Do not need to come to the Veterans Memorial Medical Center.

asr-000396
00:48:30.160 --> 00:48:45.780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: They have a scope that before the spread of the veteran services through the Valor Clinics, only 6% of the veterans were able to avail of medical treatment.

asr-000397
00:48:46.460 --> 00:48:54.720
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we have reported to the president that the structure itself of the medical center is a cause for high infection rates.

asr-000398
